# Prettier's remit is `apps/web` and `apps/functions` — the two TypeScript surfaces — and
# this file is what makes that true even for someone who runs `npx prettier --write .`
# from the repository root (docs/07-infra-deploy.md#formatting-and-linting).
#
# `docs/` and the root markdown are hand-wrapped prose whose tables are aligned for
# reading in a terminal; reflowing eleven design documents produces a diff that says
# nothing. `apps/api` is formatted by `ruff format` and `infra/` by `terraform fmt` —
# each of those is the authority on its own language, and a second formatter with a
# different opinion would just fight it.
#
# gitignore syntax: exclude everything, then re-admit each path, re-excluding each
# directory along the way so the negation can reach inside it.
/*
!/apps
/apps/*
!/apps/web
!/apps/functions

# `apps/web/.prettierignore` is not read from here — Prettier only loads the one in the
# working directory — so the entries that are about content rather than about layout are
# repeated. Generated cross-language fixtures, which the next `dev.sh gen-*-vectors` run
# would rewrite anyway, and prose.
/apps/web/src/lib/ordering-vectors.json
/apps/web/src/lib/session-event-vectors.json
/apps/web/**/*.md
